<div class='page-hero'><div><h1 class='hero-title'>05 · IN — 功能性包容、状态容器、吸收与向内坍塌<span class='hero-badge'>📖 EPE Ch.2 §4 & Ch.4</span></h1><p class='hero-sub'>IN: Functional Containment, Absorption, Participation & Collapse</p></div><div style='font-size:0.88em;color:#475569;font-weight:600;'>共 <b>246</b> 个独立义项 • <b>738</b> 句中英对照例句</div></div>
<details class='epe-book-drawer' open><summary class='epe-drawer-bar'><span>📚 《English Prepositions Explained》(Seth Lindstromberg) 原著核心精讲 — Chapter 2 (§4 IN/INTO, §5 INWARD) & Chapter 4 (In, on¹, out, into)</span><span style='font-size:0.84em;color:#6366f1;font-weight:600;'>点击收起 / 展开原书理论图式 ▾</span></summary><div class='epe-drawer-grid'><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>🧭 原著空间与功能核心图式 (Core Schema)</div><div><b>三维/二维边界包围与「功能性包容 (Functional Containment)」</b>：EPE Ch.4 §2.3 揭示了一个极其深刻的认知事实——我们使用 IN 不仅看几何包围，更看<b>容器是否发挥了限制主体不掉落、不逃逸的功能</b>（如高出果盘边缘的香蕉仍说 <i>in the bowl</i>，倒扣的碗困住烟雾说 <i>smoke in a bowl</i>，手握高尔夫球杆只包住 5% 仍说 <i>in his hands</i>）。</div><div class='epe-box-title' style='margin-top:12px;'>📝 原书典型语料例句 (Authentic Examples from EPE)</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>The bowl is holding the smoke in.</i> (功能性包容：阻止烟雾逃逸) [Ch.4 §2.3 Fig.4.2]</div><div class='epe-quote-chip'>📌 <i>I was a young man with more on his mind than in it.</i> (<i>on one's mind</i> 是沉重心理负担，<i>in one's mind</i> 是脑海容器中的想法) [Ch.3 (27)]</div></div><div class='epe-box-card'><div class='epe-box-title'>⚖️ 原书近义小品词深度辨析与隐喻机制 (Key Contrasts & Metaphors)</div><ul class='epe-contrast-list'><li><b>IN vs INTO (Ch.2 §4.2)</b>：IN 聚焦于<b>静态包容结果</b>，而 INTO 聚焦于<b>跨越边界的动态过程与撞击力</b>（如 <i>walk in the door</i> 是从门洞走进房间，而 <i>walk into the door</i> 是砰地撞在门板上！且抽象宾语如 <i>break into a conversation / look into a complaint</i> 只能用 INTO）。</li><li><b>IN vs INSIDE / WITHIN (Ch.4 §3.1)</b>：INSIDE 强调 100% 几何完全包裹且更口语有力；WITHIN 语域高雅正式，多用于抽象制度或时间（<i>within the political system</i>）。</li><li><b>状态与语言即容器 (Ch.4 §4)</b>：情绪、困境、恋情、话语均被实体化为空间容器（<i>in love/trouble/debt/denial; put thoughts into words</i>）。</li></ul></div></div></details>

